    {
      "id": "l02-past-simple",
      "title": "Past simple: verbos regulares e irregulares",
      "summary": "Acciones terminadas: la terminación -ed, el auxiliar did y los irregulares más usados.",
      "minutes": 24,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "kind": "concepto",
          "text": "El **past simple** cuenta acciones **terminadas** en un momento del pasado: «I studied yesterday», «They built the bridge in 1998». Es igual para **todas las personas**: no hay s de tercera persona.",
          "title": "Para qué sirve"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Forma",
            "Estructura",
            "Ejemplo"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Afirmativa",
              "sujeto + verbo en pasado",
              "She worked. / She went."
            ],
            [
              "Negativa",
              "sujeto + did not (didn't) + verbo base",
              "She didn't work. / She didn't go."
            ],
            [
              "Pregunta",
              "Did + sujeto + verbo base?",
              "Did she work? / Did she go?"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "kind": "importante",
          "text": "Con **did** el verbo vuelve a la **forma base**: «Did you **go**?», «I didn't **go**». Decir «Did you went?» o «I didn't went» es el error más común: el pasado ya lo marca did.",
          "title": "Did + forma base"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Regla de los regulares",
            "Ejemplos"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "General: + ed",
              "work → worked; play → played"
            ],
            [
              "Termina en e: + d",
              "use → used; live → lived"
            ],
            [
              "Consonante + y: ied",
              "study → studied; carry → carried"
            ],
            [
              "Consonante – vocal – consonante acentuada: duplica",
              "stop → stopped; plan → planned"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "La -ed suena",
            "Cuándo",
            "Ejemplos"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "t",
              "Tras sonidos sordos (p, k, s, sh, ch, f)",
              "worked (uérkt), stopped, finished"
            ],
            [
              "d",
              "Tras sonidos sonoros y vocales",
