    {
      "id": "l03-past-continuous",
      "title": "Past continuous y la combinación con el past simple",
      "summary": "Lo que estaba pasando cuando algo ocurrió: was / were + -ing, when y while.",
      "minutes": 14,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "formula",
          "expression": "sujeto + was / were + verbo-ing",
          "caption": "Past continuous"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "kind": "concepto",
          "text": "El past continuous es el **telón de fondo** (una acción en desarrollo) y el past simple es **lo que interrumpe**: «I **was studying** when the lights **went** out» (estaba estudiando cuando se fue la luz).",
          "title": "Fondo e interrupción"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Conector",
            "Va con",
            "Ejemplo"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "when",
              "La acción corta (past simple)",
              "We were pouring concrete **when** it started to rain."
            ],
            [
              "while",
              "La acción larga (past continuous)",
              "**While** we were measuring, the level fell."
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Inglés",
            "Español"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "What were you doing at 8 p.m.?",
              "¿Qué estabas haciendo a las 8 p. m.?"
            ],
            [
              "I was working on my project.",
              "Estaba trabajando en mi proyecto."
            ],
            [
              "They weren't listening.",
              "No estaban escuchando."
            ],
            [
              "While the truck was reversing, the wall collapsed.",
              "Mientras el camión retrocedía, el muro colapsó."
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "quiz",
          "question": "Completa: «I (…) when you called.»",
