    {
      "id": "l04-futuro",
      "title": "El futuro: will, going to y present continuous",
      "summary": "Tres maneras de hablar del futuro y cuándo usar cada una.",
      "minutes": 16,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Forma",
            "Estructura",
            "Se usa para",
            "Ejemplo"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "**will**",
              "will + verbo base (negativo: won't)",
              "Decisiones del momento, predicciones, promesas, hechos futuros",
              "I'll help you. / It will rain tomorrow."
            ],
            [
              "**be going to**",
              "am / is / are + going to + verbo base",
              "Planes ya decididos e intenciones; predicciones con evidencia",
              "I'm going to study tonight. / Look at the clouds: it's going to rain."
            ],
            [
              "**present continuous**",
              "am / is / are + verbo-ing",
              "Citas y planes ya organizados",
              "We're meeting the client on Friday."
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "kind": "concepto",
          "text": "**Will** = lo decido ahora o lo predigo. **Going to** = ya lo tenía pensado. «The phone is ringing — I'**ll** answer it» (decisión del momento). «I'**m going to** call him later» (ya lo había planeado).",
          "title": "La diferencia"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Inglés",
            "Suena como",
            "Español"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "tomorrow",
              "tumórou",
              "mañana"
            ],
            [
              "next week / month / year",
              "nekst uík / manz / íer",
              "la próxima semana / mes / año"
            ],
            [
              "in two days",
              "in tu deis",
              "en dos días"
            ],
            [
              "soon",
              "sun",
              "pronto"
            ],
            [
              "later",
              "léiter",
              "más tarde"
            ],
            [
              "tonight",
              "tunáit",
              "esta noche"
            ]
          ],
          "caption": "Expresiones de futuro"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Inglés",
            "Español"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "The project will take six months.",
              "El proyecto tomará seis meses."
            ],
            [
              "Will you be at the meeting? — Yes, I will.",
              "¿Estarás en la reunión? — Sí."
            ],
            [
              "We are going to build a retaining wall.",
              "Vamos a construir un muro de contención."
            ],
            [
              "It won't work.",
              "No va a funcionar."
            ],
            [
              "I am presenting my project tomorrow.",
              "Presento mi proyecto mañana."
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "kind": "nota",
          "text": "Después de **when, if, before, after, as soon as** no se usa will, aunque se hable del futuro: «I will call you **when I arrive**» (no «when I will arrive»)."
        },
